---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LandingSignal from "../components/LandingSignal.astro";
---

<BaseLayout description="Two stations can be correct and still disagree. Follow their events through illustrated essays and deterministic labs on concurrency and causal history.">
  <LandingSignal />

  <div class="landing-reading">
    <section aria-labelledby="inspect-title">
      <h2 id="inspect-title">What the atlas lets you inspect</h2>
      <p>
        A message hasn't arrived. Is the other station behind, or did it make
        a change you haven't seen? Follow the evidence each replica has, and
        see where its view ends.
      </p>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Replicas</dt>
          <dd>Compare what each station holds without pretending that either can see the whole system.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Messages</dt>
          <dd>Deliver, delay, or duplicate an update. Watch which observations reach the other station.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Clocks</dt>
          <dd>Separate an event's counter from the causal order you can prove.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Context</dt>
          <dd>Read the record of events a replica has observed, including the ones it has removed.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Merge results</dt>
          <dd>Find out which concurrent changes survive when the stations exchange what they know.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="trail-title">
      <h2 id="trail-title">One trail, seven connected ideas</h2>
      <p>
        Start with a local event and work toward structures that preserve
        concurrent changes. Dots and causal context is the first published
        sheet; the rest of this trail is planned.
      </p>
      <ol class="learning-trail" aria-label="First-release learning sequence">
        <li><span>Local history</span> <span class="status">Planned</span></li>
        <li><span>Partial order</span> <span class="status">Planned</span></li>
        <li><span>Lamport clocks</span> <span class="status">Planned</span></li>
        <li><span>Vector clocks</span> <span class="status">Planned</span></li>
        <li><a href="/atlas/dots-and-causal-context/">Dots and causal context</a> <span class="status">Read now</span></li>
        <li><span>Multi-value registers</span> <span class="status">Planned</span></li>
        <li><span>Observed-remove sets</span> <span class="status">Planned</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="read-title">
      <h2 id="read-title">Read it or run it</h2>
      <p>
        Read the explanation, diagrams, and field notes without JavaScript.
        Each sheet gives you the argument and the references, whether you
        touch a control or not.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you want to test your understanding, run the browser lab. Create
        an event, hold back a message, then inspect the result. The same
        sequence of actions produces the same trace, so you can return to
        the exact step where your prediction went wrong.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="final-entry">
      <a class="atlas-entry" href="/atlas/dots-and-causal-context/">Read dots and causal context</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .landing-reading {
    max-width: var(--measure-reading);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  h2 {
    max-width: 24ch;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  dl {
    margin-block: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  dl > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding-block: var(--space-4);
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .learning-trail {
    padding-inline-start: 1.5rem;
    margin-block: var(--space-6) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
  }

  .learning-trail li {
    padding: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-3) var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  .learning-trail li::marker {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .learning-trail .status {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: var(--space-4);
  }

  .final-entry {
    margin-block: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  @media (width < 48rem) {
    :global(.site-main:has(> .landing-signal)) {
      padding-block-start: var(--space-4);
    }

    dl > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-1);
    }
  }
</style>
